# endpaper workspace

Plain Markdown files with YAML frontmatter, no database; every command below is non-interactive and produces stable, parseable output.

## Layout

```
.endpaper/config.toml      workspace marker, do not edit
meetings/YYYY/MM/          one markdown file per meeting
notes/YYYY/MM/             one markdown file per typed or untyped note
notes/daily/YYYY/MM/       one markdown file per day, named YYYY-MM-DD.md
tasks.md                   one checkbox line per task, at the workspace root
```

## Frontmatter

Every file in `meetings/` and `notes/` starts with exactly these six keys (`id` prefixed `meeting_`/`note_`, `type` `""` when untyped, `tags` `[]`):

```yaml
---
id: meeting_20260728_a1b2c3d4
type: "standup"
title: "Q3 planning"
tags: ["platform"]
created: 2026-07-28T09:14:00
updated: 2026-07-28T09:14:00
---
```

**Links**: an ordinary markdown link, `[text](path#id)` -- `#id` is authoritative and never
changes; the path is computed by endpaper and repaired on save. Write links with no path, e.g.
`[Q3 planning](#meeting_20260728_a1b2c3d4)`.

## Tasks

One checkbox line per task in `tasks.md`, metadata in a trailing HTML comment (invisible in
any markdown viewer). `[ ]` open, `[x]` done; a bare `- [ ] ...` gets an `id` on the next scan:

```
- [ ] send the vendor comparison <!-- id:task_a1b2 tags:procurement links:meeting_20260728_a1b2c3d4 -->
```

## Commands

```bash
endpaper meeting new "Q3 planning" --type standup --tag platform
endpaper meeting list --json --type standup --tag platform --since 2026-07-01
endpaper note today                       # note new/note list take the same flags as meeting new/list
endpaper task add "send the vendor comparison" --type followup --tag procurement
endpaper task list --json --all --type followup --tag procurement  # --done: completed only
endpaper task done task_a1b2                               # endpaper task undone task_a1b2
endpaper links <id> [--json] [--direction out|in|both]     # what it points at / is pointed at by
endpaper links check [<path>...] [--json]                  # report stale/dead links
endpaper links heal  [<path>...] [--json] [--dry-run]      # repair stale links; dead ones untouched
endpaper config assistant [<value>] [--json]                # get/set the /ai assistant
```

`--tag` is repeatable, the supported way to attach tags -- an unquoted `#tag` is eaten by the shell.

Exit codes: `0` success · `1` not found · `2` usage error · `3` workspace error; diagnostics to stderr, data to stdout, never interleaved.
